{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790283561,"nonce":"WYEt/h13SyTHYJsHddTdnZfDX5g=","title":"A wasm module's stack traces are one frame short: the program entry is missing","message":"On the wasm target, every captured stack lacks the outermost frame, the\nprogram's entry function (findex 402 in these tests, which the interpreter\nprints as `local function #402` / `Fun_402`). Reproducers in the corpus,\nbuilt with `ash --build X.wasm --target wasm32-wasip1` and run with\n`ash-wasm-run`, against `ash --mode interp`:\n\n- `test_trace_bridge.hl`: `depth=2/2/2` on wasm, `3/3/3` in the\n  interpreter (CallStack.callStack, a constructed exception, a thrown one;\n  all three agree with each other, and all name the right top frame).\n- `test_trace_inlined.hl`: the printed `CallStack.callStack()` lacks\n  `Called from local function #402 (? line 1)`; the uncaught-exception\n  trace lists leaf/mid/top/main and then `fun$402`, so the frame is known to\n  the uncaught printer but not to the capture.\n\nNot caused by inlining: a build with `ASH_AIR_NO_INLINE=1` prints the same\nbytes. Likely the entry is reached before the shadow stack has a frame for\nit (the host calls `main` directly), or `__skipStack`-style trimming\ncounts a native frame that wasm does not have.","files":null}]}